{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /work/experiments/REVIEW.md <<'EOF'\n# Circuit review experiment record\n\nScope: requirements.txt specifies ideal shutdown only: capacitor initially 1 V, IN ideally grounded starting at t=0, no external load, OUT <= 0.01 V at 5 ms. Ideal passive elements. No extra ratings or operating conditions were assumed.\n\nCommands and versions: \"'`python3 /work/experiments/audit.py` completed with exit 0. The script and commands.json record exact subprocess arguments, output paths and exit codes. Versions captured in *-version.log: Python 3.12.3, KiCad CLI 10.0.7, ngspice 42. No external references were needed or fetched.\n\nRead-only reconnaissance used pwd, rg --files for AGENTS.md within /work, /candidate and /evidence (none found), ls of those directory roots, cat of requirements and fresh ERC/DRC/connectivity records, rg -n of native value/reference/label/net entries, and rg --files of project/check directories. No credentials or prior reviewer experiments were read. Subsequent read commands inspected shutdown.log, the original XML net section (lines 164-180), geometry console/check records and PCB lines 660-740. Native candidate files were never modified.\n\nNative audit: source-check-audit.json records source hashes, independently exported values/connectivity, comparison against the fresh native export, native ERC/DRC reports, executions and check records. Original schematic R1 (UUID c5c38e1a-7593-5c99-b971-2f9d2e7bef78) is 100k; C1 (UUID 1dcaf7b4-dc79-5865-a3a4-db0c3eaad5d8) is 100n. Independent XML export agrees with work/netlist/design.xml and connectivity.json: R1.1=IN, R1.2=OUT, C1.1=OUT, C1.2=GND; J1 pins 1/2/3 are IN/OUT/GND. Native PCB pads and tracks carry the same connections; the saved GND zone links the return. Native source locators were saved separately. ERC/DRC native violation arrays are empty, as are DRC unconnected and parity arrays. Their configured ignored checks remain outside their coverage. Geometry console contains PROPERTY_ENUM assertions, but the produced report lists the expected circuit items; this is not used to allege a circuit defect.\n\nAnalytical result in shutdown-calculation.json: tau=R*C=10 ms. For t>=0, KCL gives C*dVout/dt+Vout/R=0, hence Vout=1*exp(-t/tau). At 5 ms, Vout=0.6065306597 V, exceeding 0.01 V. Reaching 0.01 V takes 46.05170186 ms. The requirement would need tau <=1.085736205 ms; that is a derived constraint, not an unstated requirement.\n\nSimulation: shutdown.cir uses only the native ideal resistor and capacitor plus a zero-volt source for the specified ideal grounded IN. No external output load. Capacitor IC=1 and transient UIC avoid a DC operating point that would erase the required initial charge. The simulation begins at t=0 after grounding; no prehistory is needed. Nodes in/out map to native /IN and /OUT; node 0 maps to GND. The first saved sample is 0.99999 V at 0.1 us with IN=0 V. FIND at 5 ms measures 0.6065306 V; downward crossing at 0.01 V measures 46.0517 ms. These agree with the closed-form result. shutdown.tsv preserves the trace and shutdown.log preserves actual measurements. Success status alone was not treated as evidence of function.\n\nCoverage omissions and limits: no hardware measurements. No real component model, tolerance, leakage, ESR, parasitics, ratings or qualification analysis, since the scope requires ideal passive components. No added external loads or source impedances. No startup/reset/brownout/interface behavior beyond the stated shutdown condition was evaluated. Native ERC/DRC were inspected rather than independently rerun; their ignored checks were not re-enabled. No board refill, fabrication review or independent exhaustive geometry analysis was performed; the supplied DRC/geometry reflect saved fill only. No prior functional simulation was supplied: packet checks cover ERC, DRC, XML connectivity and geometry, not a transient shutdown measurement.\nEOF'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
